      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It turns out I'd really like to have locked rotation in desktop mode with mouse and keyboard too when being seated in a station. This allows using the mouse input to control e.g. a vehicle/mech/aircraft and use the player head as camera without needing a camera override and also having the correct position of the audio listener.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-11T18:41:43.551Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the only way to prevent players from turning when e.g. using a thumbstick is to have them use a station. If I wanted to use the thumbstick input for something else without a station this I would have to rely on teleportating him every update.\nIdeally we could use the Immobilze function in Udon with the following 4 options: 'Mobil' (or off), 'Translation', 'Rotation' and 'Both'. For desktop players that are currently using mouse and keyboard 'Rotation' should have no effect. If they used a controller on the other hand it should be active. Opening a menu would unlock rotation for desktop players with controllers for obvious reasons (I'd also have a usecase for locked rotation in desktop mode with mouse and keyboard but I don't thing this would even be considered).\nAdditionally maybe a bool option called 'AutoClearOnRespawn' or similar would be nice, although this could be done in Udon too...",
